{
  "name": "640. On Vertex and Bedrock a virtual key with no storage or topic list names none (cloud names default-deny) [SERIAL]",
  "description": "TXE-7705. Local fixture regression, no live provider call: run with providerErrorFixture=1 against the gateway of tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json, whose bedrock key sends Converse to tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs. Vertex and Bedrock read, write and publish to the storage and topics a request names with the operator's own cloud identity. A virtual key with no allowed_storage_prefixes may name no storage there, and one with no allowed_pubsub_topics no topic: the gateway refuses with 400 caller_unsupported_parameter, error.param storage_location or pubsub_topic, naming the list, before any provider call. A key with a list keeps working as TXE-7088 made it (folder 496). Vertex has no fixture host; its rows are unit tests (plugins/governance/cloudresources_test.go), the same check. 640.1 and 640.2 create a key with no lists and a key limited to s3://bifrost-fixture-bucket/tenant-a and one topic, both on Bedrock. 640.3 to 640.6 are the key with no list naming storage: an s3:// image, its https URL, an s3Location in an extra param and a batch input file, each a 400. 640.7 is the same key naming a topic, a 400. 640.8 serves that key when it names nothing. 640.9 serves the listed key inside its list, and 640.10 refuses it outside with 403, as before. 640.11 reads what reached Bedrock: the two served chats, the second with its object as an s3Location. 640.12 and 640.13 delete the keys.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "640.1 [setup] virtual key A (no storage or topic list) on Bedrock",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "  return;",
              "}",
              "pm.collectionVariables.unset('denyVkOpen'); pm.collectionVariables.unset('denyVkOpenId');",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixtureUrl') + '/__reset', method: 'POST' }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('the fixture was reset', function () { pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null); pm.expect(res.code).to.equal(200); });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('the virtual key was created', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code, pm.response.text()).to.equal(200); });",
              "var created = (pm.response.json() || {}).virtual_key || {};",
              "pm.test('it has an id and a value', function () { pm.expect(created.id, pm.response.text()).to.be.a('string').and.not.equal(''); pm.expect(created.value, pm.response.text()).to.be.a('string').and.not.equal(''); });",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('denyVkOpen', created.value || ''); pm.collectionVariables.set('denyVkOpenId', created.id || '');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"name\":\"harness-640-a-{{$guid}}\",\"provider_configs\":[{\"provider\":\"bedrock\",\"weight\":1,\"allowed_models\":[\"*\"],\"key_ids\":[\"*\"]}]}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/governance/virtual-keys",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "governance",
            "virtual-keys"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
